{"id": "EUVD-2026-76261", "enisaUuid": "3b50e74c-7bb7-39f7-9a6f-0043aaf4c0cf", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7615: avoid waiting for mac work under the mt76 mutex\n\nmt7615_suspend() acquired the mt76 mutex and then called\ncancel_delayed_work_sync() on mac_work.  mt7615_mac_work() acquires the\nsame mutex via mt7615_mutex_acquire() at the top of the worker, so if\nmac_work is already running and blocked on the mutex, the suspend path\ndeadlocks waiting for the work it holds the mutex against.\n\nFlush scan_work and mac_work before taking the mutex, matching the\nsuspend paths in mt7921 and mt7925.  scan_work only takes the mt76\nspinlock, but moving it keeps the sequence consistent.  This also keeps\nmac_work from running over an already suspended HIF, which the previous\nsplit (async cancel under the lock, sync cancel after release) would\nhave allowed.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:42:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:45:22", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/36c73b86a09f0e51c0f81a75c8945b6c5557ff27", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/33d29aeb4c0eede92622a7d04ea492b94c30f089", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ef2ec8b537c3a54e241d693bd03016f80d0d4484", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3114d479f2a1d31b2e6214c395794c6e5715e579", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4506e229b2e468b8c64bcf52c50c41a3bf2e633e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/44be85af3e1772ffb3332feafedad2a73b22854c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bda8324270b1ac91bfba1df8928e0570e29759e8"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80938", "GHSA-pv6c-cxx7-759w"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1397b806-f008-37c1-8715-6872423148a3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c6bf20109a3fae92402cb76ad709ec5256bcd169 <ef2ec8b537c3a54e241d693bd03016f80d0d4484"}, {"id": "21b621fc-f3b4-35ec-909d-4dc17b86c66b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": 